Experiment: Qwen3.8-2B Linux ANE performance parity
Date: 2026-08-29
Contract: benchmarks/qwen38-2b-contract.json
Required targets: Linux ANE >= 0.95x macOS ANE steady state; Linux ANE >= 1.05x Linux CPU median; Linux ANE versus Linux CPU ratio CI95 lower bound > 1.0x.

Verified macOS reference data:
- Instrumented two-token run after one warmup: 0.4380809170015709 seconds.
- Time to first token: 0.2901463750004041 seconds.
- Prefill: 14.91380747661077 tokens/second.
- Decode: 15.285986554316986 tokens/second.
- Ten-prompt one-run corpus mean end-to-end: 56.34133201670011 seconds.
- Ten-prompt mean time to first token: 51.53428760429961 seconds.
- Ten-prompt mean decode: 16.74448671344259 tokens/second.

Verified Linux custom-path data:
- Hybrid ANE one-token check: steps=7.515 seconds, logits=7.821 seconds.
- CPU one-token check: steps=3.114 seconds, logits=2.568 seconds.
- Both checks generated token 11.
- The Linux path keeps RMSNorm, activations, recurrent state, attention, and logits on the host.

Missing measurements:
- No complete Linux ANE-only Qwen graph exists.
- No matched ten-repetition Linux ANE corpus exists.
- No paired confidence intervals, cold starts, peak memory, or full ANE-only submission count exist.
- The bounded macOS 100-prompt attempt timed out after 900 seconds before writing artifacts.

Conclusion: the performance targets are not met or validated. The current numbers describe a hybrid Linux path and a macOS reference, not the required ANE-only comparison. A raw Qwen HWX or equivalent Linux-loadable artifact is required before this benchmark can proceed.
